    title: "韓國「全民創業」計畫個資外洩：5,000名入選者核心創意與評審意見遭竊",
    summary: "韓國政府主導的「全民創業」大型海選計畫，在吸引6.3萬人參與後，於6月17日爆發個資外洩事件。據報導，約5,000名第一階段入選者的敏感個資，包括核心創意摘要與評審意見，遭到外洩。外洩的證據來自於參賽者收到來自特定顧問公司的行銷郵件，該郵件精準掌握了參賽者的暱稱和合格狀態等非公開資訊，引發個資非法販售的懷疑。韓國中小企業暨新創事業部已聯合KISA與國家警察廳，針對相關IP位址展開調查。初步調查指出，此次事件可能源於一家AI解決方案供應商遭駭客攻擊，駭客透過系統後臺規避權限審查，並利用非正常API呼叫竊取了加密資料。事件的最終調查結果仍有待進一步釐清，但已凸顯政府主導大型計畫在個資保護上的重大風險。",
    tags: ["韓國", "個資外洩", "全民創業", "AI 供應商", "數據安全", "政府計畫"],
    title_en: "Leak of Personal Data from South Korea's 'National Entrepreneurship' Program: Core Ideas and Judging Feedback of 5,000 Selected Participants Stolen",
    summary_en: "A data leak incident occurred on June 17th during South Korea's government-led 'National Entrepreneurship' large-scale selection program, which attracted 63,000 participants. Reports indicate that sensitive personal data belonging to approximately 5,000 participants selected in the first phase, including core creative summaries and judging feedback, was leaked. Evidence of the leak came from marketing emails sent to participants by a specific consulting firm, which contained non-public information such as the participants' nicknames and qualification status, raising suspicions of illegal data sale. The Small and Medium Business and Startups Agency of Korea has joined forces with KISA and the National Police Agency to investigate the related IP addresses. Preliminary investigations suggest that the incident may have originated from an AI solution vendor being attacked by hackers, who bypassed permission checks through the system backend and stole encrypted data using abnormal API calls. The final investigation results are still pending clarification, but the incident highlights significant risks regarding personal data protection in large-scale government-led programs.",
