    id: "20260626-033",
    trackers: ["security"],
    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "微軟警告：針對飯店業的「照片ZIP檔」釣魚活動，植入Node.js後門",
    summary: "微軟指出，自 2026 年 4 月起，歐洲和亞洲的飯店及住宿業正遭受一場利用照片主題 ZIP 檔案的釣魚活動。攻擊者透過偽裝成「預訂經理 (Booking Manager)」的郵件，以房客投訴、檢查警告等為誘餌，誘騙目標下載包含惡意捷徑的 ZIP 檔案。該惡意檔案在開啟後會執行 PowerShell，利用 BigInt 算術解密隱藏的下載 URL，將 Node.js 運行時和 JavaScript 植入程式（被追蹤為 TonRAT）下載到用戶空間。植入程式透過 TON 區塊鏈 API 解析 C2 網域，並建立加密 WebSocket 通道。攻擊後，植入程式會向非標準埠（如 8443、8445 等）發出信標，並執行了地理位置檢查和強制關機等行為。修復時必須同時處理 RunOnce 和 Node.js 的持久化路徑，並檢查接待、預訂和前台系統。微軟尚未確認有資料外洩或勒索軟體攻擊。",
    tags: ["微軟", "釣魚攻擊", "Node.js", "TonRAT", "飯店業", "PowerShell", "ZIP檔"],
    title_en: "Microsoft Warns: 'Photo ZIP' Phishing Campaign Targets Hospitality Industry, Implanting Node.js Backdoor",
    summary_en: "Microsoft has pointed out that since April 2026, the hospitality and accommodation sectors in Europe and Asia have been facing a phishing campaign utilizing photo-themed ZIP files. Attackers are using emails disguised as 'Booking Managers,' employing lures such as guest complaints or inspection warnings, to trick targets into downloading ZIP files containing malicious shortcuts. Upon opening, the malicious file executes PowerShell, which uses BigInt arithmetic to decrypt a hidden download URL, subsequently downloading a Node.js runtime and JavaScript implant (tracked as TonRAT) into the user space. The implant parses the C2 domain using the TON blockchain API and establishes an encrypted WebSocket channel. Following the attack, the implant emits beacons to non-standard ports (such as 8443, 8445, etc.) and performs actions like geolocation checks and forced shutdowns. Remediation requires simultaneously addressing persistence paths for RunOnce and Node.js, and checking reception, booking, and front-desk systems. Microsoft has not confirmed any data leakage or ransomware attacks.",
    tags_en: ["Microsoft", "Phishing Attack", "Node.js", "TonRAT", "Hospitality Industry", "PowerShell", "ZIP File"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Hacker News", url: "https://thehackernews.com/2026/06/microsoft-warns-of-photo-zip-phishing.html", lang: "EN" }
    ]
