    summary_en: "This article reports that after significantly raising product prices recently, Apple has added the MacBook Neo to its official Certified Refurbished store. This store offers products that have undergone rigorous refurbishment, come with a one-year limited warranty, and a 14-day return policy. However, the article points out that because Apple's official price increases have not been fully reflected across all channels, consumers may find that buying a brand-new MacBook Neo on Amazon could still be cheaper than the price at the Apple Refurbished store, resulting in greater savings. For example, the price for the 256GB model on Amazon ($589) is even lower than the price at the Apple Refurbished store ($599). Therefore, the article advises consumers to pay attention to new model deals on Amazon rather than directly purchasing Apple refurbished products.",
    tags_en: ["Apple", "MacBook Neo", "Refurbished Products", "Amazon", "Price War"],
    sources: [
      { name: "9to5Mac", url: "https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/26/apple-now-sells-refurbished-macbook-neo-but-you-probably-shouldnt-buy-it", lang: "EN" }
    ]
