    title: "Setracker2 Android App 存在 CVE-2026-9219 漏洞：透過 IMEI 預測註冊 ID 實現越權綁定",
    summary: "Setracker2 Android Companion App (com.tgelec.setracker) 的 3.1.5 版本及更早版本，存在一個可預測的註冊 ID 漏洞。此漏洞的根源在於其註冊 ID 是基於設備的 IMEI 號碼衍生出來的，且其配對系統在指派設備時缺乏額外的身份驗證機制。攻擊者若能取得目標的註冊 ID，便可利用此漏洞，任意地為屬於其他用戶的智慧手錶進行註冊或綁定。此漏洞的攻擊向量為網路（AV:N），且無需任何權限（PR:N）。修補建議是開發者應立即更新應用程式，並強化設備註冊流程，增加額外的身份驗證步驟，以防止基於 IMEI 的 ID 預測攻擊。",
    tags: ["Setracker2", "CVE-2026-9219", "Android", "IMEI", "越權綁定", "應用程式漏洞"],
    title_en: "Setracker2 Android App Contains CVE-2026-9219 Vulnerability: Privilege Escalation via IMEI-Based ID Prediction",
    summary_en: "The Setracker2 Android Companion App (com.tgelec.setracker), versions 3.1.5 and earlier, contains a predictable registration ID vulnerability. The root cause is that the registration ID is derived from the device's IMEI number, and the pairing system lacks additional identity verification mechanisms when assigning devices. If an attacker can obtain a target's registration ID, they can exploit this vulnerability to arbitrarily register or bind smartwatches belonging to other users. The attack vector for this vulnerability is network (AV:N), and it requires no privileges (PR:N). The recommended fix is for developers to immediately update the application and strengthen the device registration process by adding extra identity verification steps to prevent IMEI-based ID prediction attacks.",
    tags_en: ["Setracker2", "CVE-2026-9219", "Android", "IMEI", "Unauthorized Binding", "Application Vulnerability"],
