    summary_en: "According to Bloomberg, AI company OpenAI has hired senior Apple executive Paul Meade. Meade was responsible for the Apple Vision Pro headset and all related smart glasses programs at Apple. He will join OpenAI's hardware division to assist in developing OpenAI's future line of AI-powered devices. During his tenure at Apple, Meade led the Vision Pro hardware engineering team for seven years and oversaw Apple's efforts to develop its first smart glasses, which are expected to launch by the end of 2027. His departure is linked to recent organizational changes at Apple following high-level restructuring, particularly after Johny Srouji, head of Apple Silicon, assumed the role of hardware chief, which prompted several senior executives to adjust their positions. This move highlights the intensifying competition in the AI hardware sector, as OpenAI actively recruits top Apple talent to accelerate the development of its AI product line.",
