    summary_en: "Intel has released the latest version, 1.31, of its implicit SPMD compiler, ISPC. This version primarily targets Intel's upcoming Nova Lake processor, adding targets such as avx10.2nvl-x4, avx10.2nvl-x8, avx10.2nvl-x16, avx10.2nvl-x32, and avx10.2nvl-x64. These new targets are similar to existing Diamond Rapids targets but lack AMX functionality. Furthermore, ISPC 1.31 provides experimental support for IBM POWER8 and newer PowerPC 64-bit, although official builds currently have this feature disabled by default. In addition to the hardware target expansion, the version includes multiple performance enhancements, standard library updates, and bug fixes, improving developers' ability to use CPU and GPU resources for Single Program, Multiple Data (SPMD) programming.",
