    summary_en: "To ensure the unified and effective implementation of the Cyber Resilience Act (CRA), market regulators from various countries held the \"AdCo CRA\" meeting in Berlin. The meeting was led by the German Federal Office for Information Security (BSI) and focused on how to monitor product reporting obligations, especially concerning vulnerabilities actively being exploited and severe security incidents. The CRA requires all products with digital components to provide adequate cybersecurity assurance by December 2027. According to the meeting information, the first phase of CRA reporting obligations will take effect on September 11, 2026. At that time, product manufacturers must proactively report actively exploited vulnerabilities and severe security incidents through the developing European \"Single Reporting Platform.\" This demonstrates that the EU is establishing a strict, cross-border product safety regulatory system.",
